From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saphira forward-port <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
Date: Thu, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [FWD 7.2.9] mm/cram: demote anonymous folios onto the CRAM tier

Fwd-port of upstream ("mm/cram: demote anonymous folios onto the CRAM
tier", Gregory Price, series position 086) onto Linux 7.2.9.

Why needed: 7.2.9 shrink_folio_list() uses `struct swap_iocb *plug`
where the branch base has the 7.3-bound `struct swap_io_ctx ctx`;
only hunk 1 context refreshed (same two insertions: cram_folios list
+ do_cram_pass). Remaining hunks verbatim upstream.

Byte-identical upstream patch retained in series/ (recorded SKIP-FWD).
Verifies with git apply --check (no fuzz).

Signed-off-by: Saphira builder <builder@saphira.vm2.uk>
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index 57b6b1766dc..74fe4a6d7c5 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -1069,15 +1069,18 @@ static unsigned int shrink_folio_list(struct list_head *folio_list,
 	struct folio_batch free_folios;
 	LIST_HEAD(ret_folios);
 	LIST_HEAD(demote_folios);
+	LIST_HEAD(cram_folios);
 	unsigned int nr_reclaimed = 0, nr_demoted = 0;
 	unsigned int pgactivate = 0;
 	bool do_demote_pass;
 	struct swap_iocb *plug = NULL;
+	bool do_cram_pass;
 
 	folio_batch_init(&free_folios);
 	memset(stat, 0, sizeof(*stat));
 	cond_resched();
 	do_demote_pass = can_demote(pgdat->node_id, sc, memcg);
+	do_cram_pass = cram_can_demote(pgdat->node_id);
 
 retry:
 	while (!list_empty(folio_list)) {
@@ -1258,6 +1261,22 @@ retry:
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * CRAM read-only tier: divert eligible folios onto a CRAM
+		 * private node by migration instead of reclaiming them.  Private
+		 * anonymous folios qualify (cram_folio_eligible).  They are
+		 * mapped read-only on the tier and a write promotes the folio
+		 * off it.  This is a distinct service from the tiering demotion
+		 * above.  Migration failures are handled by the normal reclaim
+		 * path.
+		 */
+		if (do_cram_pass && cram_folio_eligible(folio) &&
+		    (thp_migration_supported() || !folio_test_large(folio))) {
+			list_add(&folio->lru, &cram_folios);
+			folio_unlock(folio);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		/*
 		 * Anonymous process memory has backing store?
 		 * Try to allocate it some swap space here.
@@ -1581,6 +1600,24 @@ keep:
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Migrate folios selected for CRAM demotion */
+	if (!list_empty(&cram_folios)) {
+		unsigned int nr_crammed = 0;
+
+		cram_migrate_to(&cram_folios, pgdat->node_id, MIGRATE_ASYNC,
+				MR_DEMOTION, &nr_crammed);
+		nr_reclaimed += nr_crammed;
+		stat->nr_demoted += nr_crammed;
+		/* Folios that could not be crammed go back on @folio_list */
+		if (!list_empty(&cram_folios)) {
+			list_splice_init(&cram_folios, folio_list);
+			if (!sc->proactive) {
+				do_cram_pass = false;
+				goto retry;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
 	pgactivate = stat->nr_activate[0] + stat->nr_activate[1];
 
 	mem_cgroup_uncharge_folios(&free_folios);
-- 
